<metadata><name>Tumalo Mountain from Dutchman Flat Sno-Park (direct west slope)</name><desc>or-central-meissner-1984:14: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.999772" lon="-121.663687"><ele>1935.4</ele><name>Dutchman Flat Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:dutchman-flat-sno-park (OSM way 559496151); both ski recordings (2020-01-09, 2019-04-20) start at the sno-park and cross the highway here; confidence: high; pdf_page: 36; quote: book start: a plowed turn-out on the right side (north) ... shortly before the first Mt. Bachelor access road (not used; see book.note)</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.005358" lon="-121.642699"><ele>2370.9</ele><name>Tumalo Mountain summit</name><desc>source: OSM peak node 357317067; both ski recordings (2020-01-09, 2019-04-20) reach it from the west; confidence: high; pdf_page: 36; book_elev_ft: 7775; quote: Top of Tumalo Mt. - 7,775'; On top of Tumalo Mt. is an open ridge</desc></wpt>
